## 6. Where to go next (recommendation)

1. **One time-boxed H2 push on the v7 line** (≤ 1 day with the box): v7 gate → Link rebuild + H2Front port → build
   under the watchdog → downstream fixes → at submit time re-snapshot and 3-way onto whichever tree is within 2 cycles
   of the head (head itself, or the best pending with `--coauthors`). Submit if every gate passes. If a v8 lands
   mid-build: finish on v7 anyway, submit for the public record (closed PRs still carry the note and the lever), then
   decide on exactly one re-port. The sub-40M crossing (§2) is the prize to watch for.
2. **Research track, no box: price G on v7 exactly** (one agent-day). If ≥ −8 survives on v7's verifier, it is the
   largest unlanded item on the board and composes with H2. Fold Exploration 1 (signer-filter tails) into its
   sign-policy obligation when Mitch opens that session.
3. **Output regardless of the crown:** chronicle v2 (H2 as a format contribution, the ≤ 2-cycle rule, the sub-40M
   bar), the Soul Sync letter, the tome holes. The chronicle skill is already public.
4. Park H2-19/5 until H2 is promoted; park W85; drop the refit lanes.

Not recommended: competing on 1–3-cycle verify golf against nine solvers with better tracers.

## 7. Box rules and Lean gotchas (hard-won)

- WSL VM 25 GB. Full `Solution` build: `tools/wsl/cfgo.sh <worktree> "Solution" "2 1" 14G 17G` (~1 h cold, 15–40 min
  incremental). Single-file capped checks: `lean/t3h2/scratch/capchk.sh REL [SECS] [LINES]` (12 GB cap); bisect a file
  by truncation: `TREE=<worktree> lean/t3h2/scratch/bisectf.sh REL LINE SECS`. Errors per file:
  `tools/wsl/errfile.py LOG NAME N`.
- Watchdog: `tools/wsl/witness.sh 15 1500 6` (kills a lean > 15 GB for 2 min or > 25 min; `~/witness.log`). Run it under
  `setsid nohup … &` from its own `wsl -- bash -c`; a bare `pkill -f witness.sh` kills the launching shell too.
- Windows-side memory pressure reaps Claude Code's background shells (not the WSL build). Use short foreground checks;
  never wait on a question overnight — pick the low-risk default and continue (8 h lost on 6–7 Oct).
- Runaway-proof patterns (each took one file to 20+ GB): `apply BitVec.eq_of_toNat_eq` (use `refine … ?_`);
  `simp only [BitVec.extractLsb'_toNat, Nat.shiftRight_eq_div_pow, pow_zero, …]` on setTop goals (explicit `rw` +
  `generalize (2:Nat)^64 = A`); `omega`/`simp` with a literal `2^64` (`generalize` first); `decide +kernel` on code
  slices past word 1024 (use `codeAt_of_window wct_newCodeAt`). `omega` cannot see `% 18446744073709551616`: rewrite
  with helper lemmas first.
- Windows C: is at 98 % (20 GB free). WSL has 864 GB free. 47 sig-golf worktrees (20 MB each, harmless) — list for Mitch
  before pruning (no bulk deletes without review). Keep: h2b, h2d, wt9v3*, cf*, bytes, a2, gate.
- Agents on the H2 Lean work were stopped by safety classifiers three times (6 Oct); the lead did those parts directly.

